    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d392">

                <pb facs="0551" n="445" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg445"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.61/114</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Davies</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 478</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1937-08-10">August 10,
                        1937</date>.<lb/>[Received August 21.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to despatches Nos. 302 and
                    383, of May 14, and June 18, 1937, respectively,<anchor n="90" xml:id="d392-f1"
                    /> from this Embassy, I have the honor to enclose a memorandum<anchor n="91"
                        xml:id="d392-f2"/> describing recent developments concerning <pb facs="0552"
                        n="446" xml:id="pg446"/> the installation of a microphone in the Spaso
                    House, the Ambassador’s residence.</p>
                <p>Since the writing of the last despatch under reference, a microphone has been
                    found and photographed but has since been removed by persons unknown. One member
                    of the Ambassador’s household who has long been under suspicion has been
                    discovered in the attic on a questionable alibi.</p>
                <p>At present investigations are being continued with a view to determining the
                    identity of the person installing the microphone.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Ambassador: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Loy W. Henderson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">First Secretary of Embassy</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
